17\. Investor Pitch (30 seconds)
================================

Millions of readers own far more books than they can read. Existing reading apps focus on tracking progress, social features, and productivity. Tsundoku serves a different emotional need: helping readers remember, organize, and enjoy their personal library in a calm, beautiful environment. Built with an ADHD-first philosophy and an obsession with simplicity, Tsundoku transforms the unread pile from a source of guilt into a source of inspiration.

18\. LLM Context
================

When suggesting features or improvements:

Prioritize:

*   fewer taps
    
*   calm UX
    
*   bookshelf-first design
    
*   visual simplicity
    
*   fast interactions
    
*   book ownership
    
*   reader delight
    

Avoid recommending:

*   streaks
    
*   gamification
    
*   achievements
    
*   badges
    
*   social feeds
    
*   follower systems
    
*   competitive metrics
    
*   productivity pressure
    
*   feature bloat
    

Every new feature should answer:

> Does this make someone's personal bookshelf feel more useful, more beautiful, or more personal?

If the answer is no, it probably doesn't belong.

